nodecode-fabric is a rewrite of esaradev's esaradev/icarus-plugin:

  https://github.com/esaradev/icarus-plugin
  commit e46cba30fb95a0b54b7c4d6c26169a424283d72b
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 esaradev (LICENSE)

The original is a Hermes Agent plugin: a folder of markdown memory entries
shared by every agent on the machine, with an entry schema (id, agent, type,
tier, summary, tags, status, assigned_to, review_of, revises, training_value),
a ranked retriever over it, and tools to write, recall, search, list pending
handoffs, curate and briefly report; on top of that it exported training pairs
and ran Together AI fine-tunes, switching the host's model config to the
result.

What was rewritten, in Common Lisp against the Nodecode cell contract: the
entry format and its frontmatter, the retriever's scoring (keyword, summary,
exact phrase, bigram and trigram overlap, tags, project, agent, recency, tier,
entry-type words, review and revision boosts) with its deduplication and
character budget, and the tools fabric_write, fabric_recall, fabric_search,
fabric_pending, fabric_brief and fabric_curate. The original's pre_llm_call
recall became a :round hook that records what the turn's own words match onto
the turn, and its session-start injection became one short standing
paragraph. The folder default is the same ~/fabric, so the cell can read a
fabric the original's plugin wrote.

What was left out, and why: the Together AI path (fabric_train,
fabric_train_status, fabric_models, fabric_eval, fabric_switch_model,
fabric_rollback_model) uploaded pairs, polled jobs and rewrote the Hermes
host's .env to point at a fine-tuned model -- host plumbing Nodecode has its
own model settings for, so only the memory itself is ported; fabric_export,
which shelled out to a bundled Python script to build JSONL pairs, is not
ported either, and fabric_curate keeps the training_value it fed. The
Obsidian formatting, the weekly report and the telemetry file are out. One behaviour
change: a query that shares no word with an entry now answers nothing, where
the original's entry-type bonus could rank an unrelated decision above zero.
